@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+# Project Context
+
+When working with this codebase, prioritize readability over cleverness. Ask clarifying questions before making architectural changes.
+
+## Project Overview
+
+TFHE-rs is a pure Rust implementation of TFHE (Torus Fully Homomorphic Encryption) for integer arithmetics over encrypted data. This is a fork of upstream tfhe-rs with FPT integration and additional apps for profiling, testing, and demos.
+
+Minimum Rust version: 1.91. Default `RUSTFLAGS="-C target-cpu=native"`.
+
+## Common Commands
+
+### Formatting & Linting
+```bash
+make fmt                    # Auto-format all code
+make check_fmt              # Check formatting without fixing
+make clippy_all_targets     # Clippy on all targets
+make check_typos            # Check for typos
+```
+
+### Pre-Commit Checks
+```bash
+make pcc                    # Full pre-commit checks (required before PR)
+make fpcc                   # Fast pre-commit checks (subset)
+```
+
+### Testing (FPGA)
+```bash
+make test_integer_fpga          # Integer tests on FPGA
+make test_integer_fpga_emulate  # Integer tests with FPGA emulation
+make test_arrays_fpga           # High-level API array tests on FPGA
+make test_arrays_fpga_emulate   # Array tests with FPGA emulation
+make test_composites_fpga       # Composites tests on FPGA
+```
+
+To run a single test: copy the cargo command printed by a `make test_*` target, then append `-- your_test_name` or modify the filter. Tests are resource-heavy; use test filters for rapid iteration.
+
+### Benchmarking (FPGA)
+```bash
+make bench_integer_fpga     # Integer benchmarks on FPGA
+make bench_erc20_fpga       # ERC20 benchmarks on FPGA
+make bench_pbs_fpga         # PBS throughput benchmarks on FPGA
+```
+
+Run `make help` to see all ~200 available targets.
+
+## Architecture
+
+### API Layers (top-down)
+
+1. **High-Level API** (`tfhe/src/high_level_api/`) — User-facing. Provides `FheUint{8..2048}`, `FheInt{8..2048}`, `FheBool`, array types. Uses `ConfigBuilder` for setup, `generate_keys()` for key creation, and `set_server_key()` for global server key context.
+
+2. **Integer API** (`tfhe/src/integer/`) — Multi-block radix representation of arbitrary-width integers, built on shortint primitives.
+
+3. **Shortint API** (`tfhe/src/shortint/`) — Operations on small encrypted integers with message/carry parameterization. Only relevant parameter set is `PARAM_MESSAGE_2_CARRY_2_KS_PBS`.
+
+4. **Core Crypto** (`tfhe/src/core_crypto/`) — Low-level primitives: Programmable Bootstrapping (PBS), key switching, FFT/NTT backends, FPGA support.
+
+### Key Feature Flags
+- Default: `["boolean", "integer"]`
+- `shortint`, `integer` — API layer selection (`integer` includes `shortint`)
+- `fpga` — FPGA hardware acceleration backend
+- `internal-keycache` — Key caching for tests/benchmarks
+- `zk-pok` — Zero-knowledge proofs
+- `__c_api`, `__wasm_api` — C and WASM bindings
+
+### Supporting Crates
+- `tfhe-csprng` — Cryptographically secure PRNG (AES-CTR based)
+- `tfhe-fft` / `tfhe-ntt` — FFT and NTT implementations
+- `tfhe-zk-pok` — Zero-knowledge proof of knowledge
+- `tfhe-benchmark` — Benchmark suite
+- `utils/tfhe-versionable` — Data versioning framework for backward compatibility
+
+### FPGA Backend
+- FPGA support enabled via the `fpga` feature flag
+- Emulation available via `fpga,emulate_fpga` features for testing without hardware
+- FPGA tests run sequentially (`--test-threads=1`) as multiple threads cannot share FPGA
+
+## Conventions
+
+### Commits
+Conventional Commits required: `type: message` (e.g., `feat: add new operation`, `fix: correct PBS`). CI auto-rejects non-compliant messages.
+
+### Branches
+Format: `{feat|fix|docs|chore}/short_description`
+
+### Data Backward Compatibility
+Types deriving `Versionize` must remain backward compatible. Adding/reordering/renaming struct fields or enum variants is a breaking change. When modifying such types:
+1. Copy the old type definition with a version suffix (e.g., `MyTypeV1`)
+2. Add it as a new variant in the `*Versions` dispatch enum
+3. Implement the `Upgrade` trait from old version to new
+4. Update the previous version's upgrade target
+
+Historical data in `utils/tfhe-backward-compat-data/` is checked on every PR.
+
+### PRs
+Rebase on `dev` branch (no merge commits). Run `make pcc` before pushing.
+
+## Rust Best Practices
+
+### Module Structure
+Organize modules by feature/functionality, not by separating types from implementations. Keep related structs, enums, and their `impl` blocks together.
+
+### Small, Cohesive Structs
+Break down complex data into smaller, composable structs. This improves borrow-checker ergonomics and API flexibility.
+
+### Use `TODO` Comments
+Mark incomplete work with `// TODO:` comments, not vague notes.
+
+
+### Builder Pattern for Complex Construction
+Use Builder for structs with many optional fields. Avoid it for simple structs with one or two constructors.
+
+### Minimal Generic Bounds on Types
+Place generic bounds on `impl` blocks or functions, not on struct/enum definitions, unless intrinsic to the type.
+
+### Collections
+- Default to `Vec` and `HashMap`. Only use specialized collections when profiling justifies it.
+- Pre-allocate with `with_capacity()` when size is known.
+
+### Error Handling
+- Use `Result<T, E>` for recoverable errors. Reserve `panic!` for programming errors.
+
+### `unsafe` Documentation
+Every `unsafe` block must have a preceding `// SAFETY:` comment explaining soundness.
